%N A395433 a(n) is the median of the odd primes less than 2n.
%C A395433 It seems that a(n) < n for n > 12. The sequence contains all odd primes and interprimes, and nothing else.
%H A395433 Ya-Ping Lu, <a href="/A395433/b395433.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 2..10000</a>
%e A395433 For n = 3, the odd primes < 2n are 3 and 5. a(3) = 4 because the median of {3, 5} is 4. a(8) = 7 because the median of odd primes < 2*8, {3, 5, 7, 11, 13}, is 7.
%t A395433 a[n_]:=Median[Select[Range[3,2n],PrimeQ]]; Array[a,67,2 ] (* _Stefano Spezia_, Sep 16 2026 *)
%o A395433 (Python)
%o A395433 from sympy import primepi, prime, nextprime
%o A395433 def A395433(n):
%o A395433     ct = primepi(2*n); hp = prime((ct+1)//2); np = nextprime(hp)
%o A395433     return (hp + np)//2 if ct%2 else np
%Y A395433 Cf. A063934, A076639.
%K A395433 nonn,new
